# Environment
.venv/
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Downloaded files, such as the tokenizer that tiktoken fetches the first time
# (.cache/tiktoken, see TOKENIZER_CACHE_DIR in ingest/chunks.py). They come from
# outside the project, are checked by their SHA-256 and are fetched again if missing.
.cache/

# Downloaded corpus and parsed layer (D-002): not versioned in git, they can be
# regenerated from data/manifest.json + ingest/. That is why every row of the
# measurement log records the download date and the snapshot hash: the commit
# alone does not reproduce an experiment.
data/raw/
data/processed/
# Same rule: t2_nodes.json is the per-node derived layer (1.8 MB, corpus text
# included), regenerable with scripts/measure_nodes.py. The measurement
# profiles ARE versioned, like data/t1_report.json.
data/t2_nodes.json
# The chunk layer (T2) follows the same rule: derived from data/processed/ by
# scripts/run_t2.py, with corpus text inside. Its profile, data/t2_chunk_profile.json,
# IS versioned.
data/chunks/
# Embeddings and runs of the dense baseline: derived from the chunk layer, the queries
# and an embedding model (ingest/embeddings.py), regenerable, and several MB each. Their
# meta.json says what produced them. The summary of a run IS versioned, in data/results/.
data/embeddings/
data/runs/
# Later versions of the acts, downloaded only to compare against the parsed snapshot
# (scripts/build_psd2_exclusions.py). Never parsed or indexed, and never in the
# ingestion manifest; their SHA-256 is recorded in the derived list.
data/reference/

# Local Claude Code config: it belongs to this machine, not to the project.
# .claude/settings.json (without "local") IS shared and can be versioned.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Internal working documents (engineering notes, decision and measurement
# records): kept outside the public repository. See "Engineering records" in
# README.md.
CLAUDE.md
docs/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# NOTE: this file IS pushed to the repo. It is a list of patterns to ignore,
# not a place to keep anything. Secrets go in .env, which is ignored above and
# therefore never leaves this machine.
